7. Release the protected session/workspace.
8. Restore only authorized permissions and services.
9. Verify session functionality.
10. Record the release event.
11. Notify affected user and stakeholders.
12. Close only after closure requirements are met.

If the incident is not cleared, relevant restrictions remain active.

Releasing a session must never erase its incident or evidence history.

